equently reported region of travel changed from the Caribbean (42%) during 2010–2014 to Asia (35%) during 2015–2017\"}]}], \"methods_quotes\": [{\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"The incidence of dengue cases among U.S. outbound travelers was calculated using denominator data from the National Travel and Tourism Office.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Travelers to Europe were excluded from the denominator because of the small number of dengue cases reported from Europe.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Travel destinations were recorded as the areas visited outside the continental United States in the 14 days before illness onset\"}], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"uncertain_fields\": []}", "type": "text"}]}